From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: up to four players, each with their own controller (Wine
 patch 0926)

On the PS5 each controller belongs to a signed-in user, and a title opens
a user's controller by that user. In xinput and dualsense modes the title
now looks at the signed-in users once a second (pw_players_ps5.c): a user
other than player 1 takes the first free place, 2 to 4, while signed in,
and their controller becomes XInput controller 1 to 3, with its own
rumble. The sink keeps a slot and a rumble for each player
(pw_wine_set_pad_at, pw_wine_pad_at, pw_wine_rumble_at,
pw_wine_set_rumble_at; the older calls are player 1's), and Wine patch
0926 makes xinput and Windows.Gaming.Input answer for all four. Keyboard
mode stays one player, so a game doesn't take player 2's controller for
its own. Player 1 keeps PC5's menus, leaving the game, the on-screen
keyboard, the light bar, the triggers and, in dualsense mode, the
DualSense a game finds.
